  "description": "Participants freely view five pavilion scenes from the 1744 album Forty Views of the Yuanmingyuan (Jiajing mingqin, Shangxia tianguang, Changchun xianguan, Xinghua chunguan, Tantan dangdang) in random order, 25 s each with a 5 s grey screen in between, then answer the study's eight post-viewing questions (six 5-point agreement items on whole-to-detail viewing and on pavilions as focal points, the painting that made the deepest impression, and which elements become visual focal points). Rebuilt from Liu, Fu, Hou & Wang (2026), Journal of Eye Movement Research 19(6): 122, using public-domain images of the same paintings from Wikimedia Commons. Analysis: medians and agreement rates per item, choice shares for the two choice questions (the paper's eye-tracking measures need an eye tracker).",
